  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Maryland received $226M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Maryland recorded 1,234 awards in the same period, with an average award size of $184K. Maryland obligations were down 99.4% year over year. National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the largest buying agency with $107M in obligations, followed by Department of Veterans Affairs with $55.5M and Department of Health and Human Services with $33.8M. THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC is the largest vendor with $85.3M in obligations. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry by obligations at $99.1M. Maryland FY22 obligations were $42.1B, FY23 obligations were $41.7B, FY24 obligations were $46.3B, FY25 obligations were $39.7B, and FY26 obligations were $37.5B. The FY2027 to date total of $226M is a partial fiscal year total and reflects obligations recorded so far in the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the FY2027 to date total and trajectory?",
        "body": "Maryland obligations are $226M in FY2027 to date, and obligations were down 99.4% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show prior full-year obligations of $42.1B in FY22, $41.7B in FY23, $46.3B in FY24, $39.7B in FY25, and $37.5B in FY26. The FY2027 figure is a partial, fiscal year to date total. Users should note the FY2027 total reflects obligations recorded so far in the fiscal year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate Maryland contracting?",
        "body": "National Aeronautics and Space Administration leads buying agencies with $107M in FY2027 to date, followed by Department of Veterans Affairs with $55.5M and Department of Health and Human Services with $33.8M. THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC is the top vendor at $85.3M, with MATOS-GRUNLEY JOINT VENTURE next at $21.4M and ARINC INCORPORATED at $10.7M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the top industry at $99.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
